questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput microservice intermittently deadlocks under load. The service utilizes a custom multi-level caching system backed by `ConcurrentHashMap`. A code audit reveals the following snippet used during cache warming:

java
@Service
public class DynamicEntityCache {
    private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Object> cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public Object getOrCompute(String key) {
        return cache.computeIfAbsent(key, k -> {
            if (k.startsWith("nested:")) {
                return "leaf-value";
            }
            return "parent:" + cache.computeIfAbsent("nested:" + k, nk -> "computed:" + nk);
        });
    }
}
